course: dictionary
lesson: 12279
title: Contrived: when it feels fake
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Contrived means seeming false and planned, not natural or believable. Something contrived looks like someone forced it to happen. «The ending of the film felt contrived.» The author tied everything up too neatly, so it did not feel real.
explain: The words around contrived give you clues. A lucky coincidence that solves every problem, or a smile that looks forced, can both be contrived. «She gave a contrived smile when she opened the present she did not like.» The smile is not real, so contrived must mean forced and fake.
explain: Contrived can also be the past form of the verb contrive. «She contrived to escape» means she managed it by being clever or tricky. «They contrived a raft from old barrels» means they made it cleverly. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «She managed to escape by being clever» still makes sense.
fact: Contrived means seeming false and planned, not natural or believable.
fact: «A contrived plot» is a story that depends on unlikely coincidences.
fact: «A contrived smile» looks forced, not real.
fact: «Contrive» is the verb; «contrived» is its past form and can mean managed cleverly or made something cleverly.
fact: As an adjective, contrived can become «more contrived», which means even more false or forced.
exercise: «The ending of the film felt contrived, because the hero was saved by a lucky coincidence.» What does contrived mean here? | Funny and very short | *Seeming false and planned, not believable | Brightly coloured | Natural and very real
exercise: «She contrived to escape from the locked room.» What does contrived mean here? | Painted the walls | Gave up and cried | *Managed to do something by being clever or tricky | Fell fast asleep
exercise: «They contrived a raft from old barrels.» What did they do with the barrels? | Broke them into little pieces | *Made a raft cleverly from them | Sold them to the shop
test: «His contrived smile told me he did not mean it.» What does contrived suggest? | *Forced and not real | Happy and bright | Very quick and sudden
test: Mia says the plot is contrived. What is she telling you? | *The story feels planned and not believable | The story is perfectly natural | The story is for babies | The story is very long
exam: «The author's coincidences were so contrived that Sam stopped believing the story.» What is the best meaning of contrived here? | *Forced, false and unbelievable | Clever and kind | Quick and funny | Old and dusty
